  "body": "Found while writing the macOS docs (#1236, PR #1237).\n\n**What happens (from the source, unconfirmed on a Mac):** edge picking adds to the selection on `mods.ctrl` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/edge_pick.rs`), while every keyboard shortcut uses egui's `modifiers.command` (Cmd on macOS). On macOS, Control-click is the system's secondary (right) click, so a Mac user likely can't Ctrl+click to add an edge chain to an operation's picks. The docs can't describe a working macOS gesture.\n\n**Done means:** add-to-selection on picks uses the platform's command modifier (`modifiers.command`: Cmd on macOS, Ctrl elsewhere) consistently with the shortcuts, or a stated alternative that works on macOS; the UI hint text says the right key per platform; pinned by a UI test with the command modifier; the docs page updated.\n",
